<x-marketing.intro eyebrow="FOR INSTITUTIONS" title="Give student potential a stronger setting.">A connected vision for academic project organisation, student collaboration and meaningful supervision — with institutional boundaries built into the architecture.</x-marketing.intro>
<section class="container section-topless"><x-ui.alert>Institutional features are planned. Memberships, institutional permissions and management tools are not yet implemented.</x-ui.alert></section>
<section class="container section"><x-marketing.heading eyebrow="ORGANISE WITH PURPOSE" title="A structure that reflects academic life.">Support the contexts where students learn and build, without treating every project or person as the same.</x-marketing.heading><div class="feature-grid"><x-marketing.feature number="01 / ACADEMIC STRUCTURE" title="Programmes & intakes.">Organise programmes and intakes, then connect classes to the academic work they support within a specific institution.</x-marketing.feature><x-marketing.feature number="02 / PROJECT ORGANISATION" title="Classes & project groups.">Future academic project groups will bring student collaboration, tasks and deliverables into a clear institutional context.</x-marketing.feature><x-marketing.feature number="03 / GUIDANCE" title="Lecturers & supervisors.">Planned role-based access will give lecturers and supervisors appropriate ways to guide work and understand project progress.</x-marketing.feature></div></section>
<section class="institution-section"><div class="container editorial-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">BOUNDARIES ARE PART OF THE DESIGN</p><h2>Connected environments.<br>Explicit access.</h2></div><div><p>Ideyra’s foundation is designed for multiple institutions. Future membership and role checks must apply within the selected institution, rather than treating a person’s access as universal.</p><p>Students keep an independent personal workspace. Institution membership must not automatically reveal personal ideas, projects or private professional drafts. Sharing and collaboration will require explicit grants.</p><p>These are architectural commitments, not implemented permission features. Institutional data and administration will be delivered in later phases.</p></div></div></section>
<x-marketing.cta title="Help shape the institutional conversation." :institution="true">Tell us about the programmes, projects and student experiences you want to support. Enquiries are securely stored for later review.</x-marketing.cta>
